<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="lt">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>{% block title %}Mokesčių Sufleris{% endblock %}</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Open+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;1,400&family=Roboto+Mono:wght@400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="build/app.css">
</head>
<body>
    {#
        "Home" shell — recreated from the real product snapshot
        (https://richkus.github.io/Richkus-MS-atkurti-bandau/), not the
        Figma reference used for content-base.html.twig. Separate base
        on purpose: content-base.html.twig stays untouched for now
        (per the user — "šitą kolkas paliekam"), and the real home page
        genuinely differs from that Figma article-page mockup — no AI
        panel, no top icon nav row, different topbar actions, a much
        longer real sidebar ("Admin dalis").

        Reuses the SAME .content-sidebar / .content-topbar CSS classes
        as the content-concept shell (identical visual treatment —
        colors, collapse-to-rail, VIBE badge) so that styling isn't
        duplicated; only the nav content differs, via these separate
        partials. Same sidebarCollapsed Alpine state/toggle mechanism.
    #}
    <div class="content-shell" x-data="contentShellState()" :class="{ 'is-sidebar-collapsed': sidebarCollapsed }">
        {% include "partials/_home-sidebar.html.twig" %}

        <div class="content-shell__main">
            {% include "partials/_home-topbar.html.twig" %}

            <div class="content-shell__scroll">
                {% block content %}{% endblock %}

                {% include "partials/_content-footer.html.twig" %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {% block javascripts %}
        <script src="build/runtime.js"></script>
        <script src="build/app.js"></script>
    {% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
